# Optional modules (Tickets / Todos / Docs / Argos / Chat)

Read `whoami.modules` (`work` / `argos` / `chat`). Same shape on `GET /ui/public`. Default all off — do not invent missing tabs or APIs.

| Flag | SPA | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `work` | `$ROOT_URL/tickets`, `/todos`, `/docs` | Top-level tabs (human only; no bygent) |
| `argos` | `$ROOT_URL/argos` | Run browser; ingest on this island; deep link `/argos/runs/{sid}` |
| `chat` | header launcher + right dock; mobile `/chat` | Org IM |

When a flag is true, browser or session cookie use of that SPA and matching `/ui/work/*`, `/ui/argos/*`, `/ui/chat/*` is allowed. Git / PR / CI / secrets stay MCP-first — do not use the browser to replace those tools.

- Argos CLI: `ARGOS_DASH_URL=$ROOT_URL`. Prefer Argos → CLI (`dash.env`).
- Open a ticket from a failing case only when **both** `work` and `argos` are true.

Fetch `whoami.skill_url` for the instance's full Optional modules text.
